  "python_code": "async def act(page):\n    \"\"\"\n    - Use the site-aware helper create_curated_collection_by_search to perform a visible-site search\n      for the keyword \"playbook\". That helper is required for site searches when available and will\n      navigate to '/' and operate the complementary-region search UI.\n    - After the helper completes (it waits for results inside role=\"main\"), locate the role=\"article\"\n      children inside role=\"main\", count them, compute the second-to-last index, and click the\n      title link inside that article's heading using a full parent->child get_by_role path.\n\n    Notes:\n    - Call .count() before .nth() to avoid indexing errors.\n    - Clicking the title link is the final action because it may navigate away from the page.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Use the knowledge-base helper to run the visible search. This helper navigates to '/'\n    # and triggers the complementary-region search UI, then waits for results to appear in role='main'.\n    await create_curated_collection_by_search(page, \"playbook\", max_results=0, resolve_links=True)\n\n    # After the helper returns, results should be rendered into role=\"main\" as article children.\n    main = page.get_by_role(\"main\")\n    articles = main.get_by_role(\"article\")\n\n    # Count before indexing to avoid locator indexing errors.\n    count = await articles.count()\n    if count == 0:\n        # No results to click; nothing to do.\n        return\n\n    # Choose second-to-last index (0-based). If fewer than 2 results, fall back to the first result.\n    target_index = count - 2 if count >= 2 else 0\n    target_article = articles.nth(target_index)\n\n    # Click the title link inside the article's heading using a full parent->child path to avoid ambiguity.\n    heading = target_article.get_by_role(\"heading\")\n    title_link = heading.get_by_role(\"link\")\n\n    # Ensure the link is visible before clicking (helps with client-side rendering delays).\n    await title_link.wait_for(state=\"visible\")\n    await title_link.click()\n",
