ion_by_search helper specifically implements the visible search widget interactions and\n     waits for results in role='main', exactly matching the task requirement to use the site's search bar. Its use\n     reduces brittle selector logic and adheres to the instructions that require using site-aware helpers when available.\n\n6) Edge cases handled:\n   - If no articles are found (count == 0), act() returns without attempting a click.\n   - If only one article is found, the code falls back to clicking the first result.\n\nSummary: The code calls the required knowledge-base helper to perform the search, then locates the second-to-last\narticle in the results and clicks its title link using accessibility-role-centric selectors and safe indexing.",
